    "title": "Panel: Does EPA's Deregulation Proposal Strike Right Balance Between Consumer Choice and Oversight? | NTD",
    "text": "The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) proposed a repeal of its long-standing “endangerment findings” of a connection between individual motor vehicle emissions and changes in the climate, according to EPA Administrator Lee Zeldin. For a deeper look at this, NTD spoke to David Blackmon, an energy policy analyst and senior contributor to Forbes, and Mike Leon, director of strategy at the Free and Equal Elections Foundation and host of the \"Can We Please Talk\" podcast.\nPanel: Does EPA's Deregulation Proposal Strike Right Balance Between Consumer Choice and Oversight?\nThe panel discussed the EPA's proposed repeal of its long-standing findings regarding car emissions and changes in the climate.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 7/30/2025, 11:08:34 PM EDT",
